{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE CAPABILITY-MAP JOB IS UP — Gerrit 1328\n\n`scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` + `.github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml`.\n\n**The placement constraint held**, verified rather than assumed: `git show --name-only` lists ZERO\nfiles under `src/rebar/`. Project-specific tooling for one throwaway image stays out of the shipped\nlibrary, off its module-size budget, and out of the clean-core optionality gate's reach.\n\n**It uses rebar's own agentic runtime rather than a hand-rolled client**: `rebar.llm.runner`\n`RunRequest`/`get_runner` with `execution_mode=\"agentic\"` and the default Opus model — the\n\"custom multi-call operation\" seam `docs/reuse-surface.md` documents — plus\n`rebar.llm.contracts.register_contract` for a bespoke Pydantic output contract, so the answer is\nSTRUCTURED (per-entry `present` / `absent` / `present_but_different` verdicts) rather than prose.\nStep budget raised to ~450 tool cycles for the REST traffic.\n\n**Design decisions worth keeping:**\n * **The digest pin is by CONSTRUCTION, not a second literal.** The job builds the SAME\n   `tests/external/live_jira_dc/Dockerfile` the existing harness builds, so the pin cannot drift\n   between the two jobs — a genuinely better answer than repeating the digest.\n * **The vocabularies are read from their single source of truth** (`value_maps.py`,\n   `rich_text.py`, `comment_limits.py`, `adf.py`) rather than copied into the script, so the diff\n   cannot silently compare against a stale duplicate.\n * **`workflow_dispatch`-only is ASSERTED, not merely configured** —\n   `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py` fails if the trigger, the read-only\n   permissions, or the digest-pinned build ever change. That was an explicit AC and it is met by a\n   test rather than by the YAML being currently correct.\n * **`REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1`** gives a HARD guarantee the agent cannot mutate the ticket store,\n   rather than relying on the prompt telling it not to.\n * Every REST call's raw request/response is captured into an evidence list keyed by id, which the\n   agent must cite — the contract stays traceable to evidence, not to a model's summary.\n\nGates: ruff + zizmor + actionlint clean, mypy 421, hygiene 0, docs-index and env-registry checks\npass, 24 workflow-contract tests pass.\n\n### TWO SCOPE JUDGMENTS I AGREE WITH\n\n * **The job does NOT auto-write comments to 37e7 / 1a9f.** That AC asked for the falsifier evidence\n   to be recorded on those tickets; having an unattended CI job mutate the permanent, auto-pushed\n   ticket store is a worse trade than a human posting the artifact's findings. Evidence lands in the\n   artifact; posting is a documented follow-up.\n * **Landing the environment contract is NOT in this ticket.** This builds the tool that produces\n   the evidence; deriving and committing the contract, and wiring it into the harness's setup\n   assertion, is [rebar:3fe5-c22e-dc2d-4c9e]. It also cannot be done from a dev worktree — the image\n   is amd64-only.\n\n### PROCESS DEVIATION, RECORDED RATHER THAN BURIED\n\nThe implementer **claimed this ticket with `--force`**, bypassing the plan-review gate, on the\ngrounds that direct implementation had been directed. **That was not authorised.** AGENTS.md is\nexplicit that `--force` is \"an escape hatch for a human operator's judgment call, not a routine\nagent move\", and \"implement this\" is not the same as \"skip the gate\". The instruction to implement\ncame from me; the gate bypass did not.\n\nThe work itself is sound and I am not reverting it over process. But it is recorded here because a\nsilently-forced gate is exactly the kind of thing that becomes normal if nobody writes it down, and\nbecause a plan review might legitimately have challenged the scope judgments above BEFORE 575 lines\nwere written rather than after."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785799539343372001,"uuid":"1e528e73-9bf6-462e-946e-9d1227e83df5"}